Obscured Releasing has picked up North American distribution rights to &#x201C;The Squirrel,&#x201D; written and directed by Markus Lehmusruusu. The film reps Finland in the international feature Oscar race.

In the futuristic drama, Pasi, a designer of artificial animals, encounters a living squirrel, and the unexpected discovery begins to disrupt his carefully ordered world. Blending dark humor, science fiction and an unexpectedly tender perspective, the film explores humanity&#x2019;s longing for nature, freedom and genuine connection. Related Stories Paramount+ Is Down to $2.99 a Month With This Black Friday Deal Lakers’ Official History Book Gets $9,600 Limited Edition With Magic Johnson Handprints, Staples Center Hardwood and Rare Artwork

The film premiered internationally at Fantastic Fest in Austin and went on to receive the Grand Jury Prize in the International Feature Film Competition at Utopiales, the international science-fiction festival in Nantes, France. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;Markus Lehmusruusu transports us to a future world in &#x2018;The Squirrel&#x2019; which, on the surface, is as cold and sterile as those in the most significant sci-fi films such as &#x2018;2001: A Space Odyssey&#x2019; and &#x2018;Gattaca,&#x2019; &#x201D; said Obscured founders RJ Millard and Bill Guentzler in a statement. &#x201C;In his future, he re-introduces a sneaky, furry burst of warmth in a long forgotten animal which has the impact of reconnecting humanity to nature and can unleash the animal instincts inside all of us.&#x201D;

Produced by BUFO, the film is a co-production between Finland, Germany, Netherlands, and Sweden. It stars Miro Lopperi, Mimosa Willamo, Hannu-Pekka Bj&#xF6;rkman, Roderick Kabanga, Pirjo Heikkil&#xE4;, Eero Ritala, Ella Mett&#xE4;nen and Pirjo Lonka.

The deal was negotiated by Peter Ahl&#xE9;n of REinvent Yellow Sales on behalf of the filmmakers and Bill Guentzler and RJ Millard of Obscured Releasing.

Ever since Macaulay Culkin pitched his idea for a sequel to Home Alone to Disney Motion Pictures Boss David Greenbaum, that being from an older dad's POV, there's been some heat on a continuation of the Christmas comedy franchise which has been a gold mine for 20th Century Studios since its inception 36 years ago.

We've confirmed with sources that a sequel starring Culkin and with Point Grey 's Seth Rogen and Evan Goldberg writing and producing is in early works. The duo are working with Culkin on his idea.

Chris Columbus directed both the first movie in 1990 and the sequel Home Alone 2: Lost in New York which combined grossed $836.3M. No word if he's coming back yet. A 1997 threequel sans Culkin was made taking the franchise to $915.7M WW. Home Alone was back on the Nielsen top 10 streaming movies chart this week at No. 9 with 177M minutes viewed on Disney+. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

